  ===== KEY QUESTION: WHY MORE CYCLES FOR BIBD? =====
  At n=7, the 3 classes all have c3=14 (same # 3-cycle vertex sets).
  The difference is in 5-cycles and 7-cycles.
  BIBD has MORE 5-cycles per 5-vertex subset because its
  3-cycle distribution is more UNIFORM across vertex pairs.
  This creates more regular sub-tournaments on 5 vertices,
  which have more Hamiltonian cycles (H_5 is maximized by regularity).

